  "issues": {
    "hx1": "On /stats, when an earlier date range's stats response arrives after a later one, the page shows the earlier range's results while the From/To fields show the newer range; triggered by changing a date twice quickly with the first request slow.",
    "hx2": "In the /stats weight-by-month table (GET /api/stats/harvests), two plants sharing a name are merged into one row with summed months, while Best plants lists them separately; triggered by creating two plants with the same name and logging harvests for both.",
    "stats-stale-summary-on-error": "On /stats, after a successful load, a failed request for a new range leaves the previous range's harvest-count summary line visible next to the error; triggered by making the API fail and changing a date.",
    "stats-blank-date-silent-default": "On /stats, clearing the From or To field drops the parameter so the server silently uses this year's start or end, leaving the field blank while results use another range or showing a 'From must be on or before To' error; triggered by clearing one field with the other set outside this year.",
    "stats-malformed-response-crash": "On /stats, a 200 stats response that is malformed, non-JSON, or missing/null fields throws an uncaught TypeError during render, leaving 'Loading stats…' stuck over the previous range's data (or the page never rendering); triggered by mocking such a response and changing a date or navigating to Stats.",
    "stats-null-fields-rendered-as-placeholders": "On /stats, a stats response with null or missing fields renders as 'null/undefined harvests from – to –', an empty Best plants section and blank table rows instead of an error; triggered by mocking a response with null fields.",
    "stats-no-request-timeout": "On /stats, the stats request has no timeout, so a hung API leaves 'Loading stats…' on screen indefinitely (often over the old range's data) with no error; triggered by making /api/stats/harvests never respond and opening the page or changing a date.",
    "stats-no-retry-after-error": "On /stats, the error state shows only a message with no Retry button, so recovering the same range requires changing a date or reloading; triggered by making /api/stats/harvests fail.",
    "stats-raw-validation-message": "On /stats, an invalid date (e.g. ?from=2026-02-30 or a 5-digit year) shows the raw Pydantic message such as 'Query.from: Input should be a valid date or datetime…' and the date input appears blank; triggered by opening such a URL or typing such a date.",
    "stats-empty-months-omitted": "On the /stats table (GET /api/stats/harvests), only months that have harvests become columns, so empty months in the chosen range are hidden and non-adjacent months appear side by side; triggered by choosing a range containing months with no harvests.",
    "stats-long-name-table-column-hides-values": "On /stats at 375 px, the white-space: nowrap plant row header makes a long plant name fill the table's visible width, pushing all month and total columns off-screen; triggered by a plant with a long unbroken name.",
    "stats-long-name-truncated-in-cards": "On the /stats Best plants cards and the dashboard top-plant card at 375 px, long plant names are cut off with an ellipsis and no way to read the full name; triggered by a plant with a long unbroken name.",
    "stats-page-horizontal-overflow-long-name": "On /stats at 375 px, a long unbroken plant name in the Best plants list does not wrap, so the whole page scrolls sideways; triggered by a plant with an 80-character name.",
    "stats-date-fields-ignore-url-changes": "On /stats, the From/To fields are read from the URL only at setup, so in-app navigation to /stats (e.g. the Stats nav link or back/forward) changes the URL but leaves the old range in the fields and data; triggered by navigating while already on a filtered /stats.",
    "dashboard-top-plant-ambiguous": "The dashboard 'Top plant this year' card shows only the plant name and links to /stats rather than the plant, so it is ambiguous when plants share a name; triggered by having two plants with the same name."
  }
}
